If a cubic intersects two horizontal lines a total of six times, you immediately know each of them gets intersected exactly thrice (because of polynomial properties). Furthermore, if you've worked with cubics, you'll know that they can have up to two humps (a local max and a local min). This is a little handwavy, but basically **we need to make our cubic as curvy as possible, so we need exactly two humps.**

