Solved with **bayern271**.

First, observe that
\begin{align*}
    \angle{YAZ} &= \angle{CAZ} 
    &= \angle{CBZ} 
    &= \angle{DBZ} 
    &= \angle{DXZ} 
    &= \angle{YXZ},
\end{align*}
so it follows that  $AXZY$  is cyclic. 

Therefore, we find that
\begin{align*}
    \angle{BWY} &= \angle{BWZ} 
    &= 180^\circ-\angle{BAZ} 
    &= 180^\circ-\angle{XAZ} 
    &= 180^\circ-\angle{XYZ} 
    &= 180^\circ-\angle{XYW},
\end{align*}
so it follows that  $BW \parallel DX.$  

Now, by Reim's Theorem, we also know that  $DY \parallel AC,$  so it results that  $BW \parallel AC.$  Therefore, this implies that  $ABZV$  is an isosceles trapezoid, so  $AB=VW,$  as desired.  $\square$

