In all cases, S-tetrominoes have an even number of red tiles and Z-tetrominos have an odd number of red tiles. A polygon P that can be tiled with S-tetrominoes thus contains an even number of red tiles, and any tiling of it using S- and Z- tetrominoes uses an even number of Z-tetrominoes.

