*Proof:* We have that  $\angle{BCH} = 90^{\circ} - \angle{CHK} = 90^{\circ} - \angle{AHM} = \angle{HAM}$ . Then  $\angle{BGH} = \angle{HAM}$  because  $BGHA$  is a parallelogram. So  $\angle{BGH} = \angle{BCH}$  and  $BGCH$  is cyclic, which implies  $\angle{CGH} = \angle{CBH}$ . Since  $\angle{ALH} = \angle{BKH}$ ,  $ALKB$  is cyclic and  $\angle{CBH} = \angle{KBH} = \angle{LAH}$ . We get  $\angle{CGH} = \angle{LAH}$ , but then  $\angle{CHG} = \angle{HLA} = 90^{\circ}$ . So,  $\triangle{GCH} \sim \triangle{ALH}$  by AA similarity.

