Note that  $AK$  and  $AM$  are isogonal, so  $\triangle BAK\sim\triangle BCM$ , so  $\frac{BK\cdot CM}{AK\cdot BC}=1$ , so  $(BK/BT_1)^2=2$ , so the answer is  $\boxed{\sqrt{2}}$ .

