Let  $CC\cap DD=T$ . I claim that  $H',I',T$  are collinear. I'm sure there's a much smarter way to do this, but here's a Menelaus "bash" motivated by length conditions. We have: 
\[(C,D;H,I)\stackrel{C}{=}(T,D;A,B)\implies \frac{CH}{CI}\div \frac{DH}{DI}=\frac{TA}{TB}\div \frac{DA}{DB}\]
and therefore
\begin{align*}
\frac{TA}{TB}\cdot \frac{H'C}{H'A}\cdot \frac{I'B}{I'C} &= \frac{TA}{TB}\cdot \frac{HA}{HC}\cdot \frac{IC}{IB} 
&= \frac{HA}{HC}\cdot \frac{IC}{IB}\cdot \frac{CH}{CI}\cdot \frac{DI}{DH} 
&= \frac{DI}{IB}\cdot \frac{HA}{DH} 
&= \frac{DC}{DB}\cdot \frac{DA}{DC} = 1
\end{align*}
proving the claim.
