\end{align*}
Note that we can shift the complex plane by  $i.$  Thus, the answer is  $\boxed{6 + 6\sqrt3}$

Rearranging,
\begin{align*}
z^4 - 6z^2 + 8z + 1 = -4(z^3 - z + 2)i &\implies z^4 +4z^3i-6z^2 - 4zi + 1 = -8(z+i) 
&\implies (z+i)^4 =-8(z+i).
\end{align*}
So, the roots, geometrically, are an equilateral triangle of side length  $2\sqrt{3}$  and its center. The sum of pairwise distances is  $\boxed{6+6\sqrt{3}.}$

