r &=e^{i\pi/3}(c-b)+b 
s &=e^{i\pi/3}(d-c)+c 
p &=e^{i\pi/3}(a-d)+d.
\end{align*}

Let  $\omega=e^{i\pi /3}$ . Thus we have 

\begin{align*}
KM=|k-m| &=\left| \dfrac{p+q}{2}-\dfrac{r+s}{2}\right| 
&=\left| \omega(b-d)+\dfrac{a+d-b-c}{2}\right| 
&=\left| \dfrac{1}{2}(a-c)+\left(\omega-\dfrac{1}{2}\right)(b-d)\right|.
\end{align*}
